---
// Sliding window counter: weight the previous window by how much of it is still inside the
// sliding window, assuming its requests were spread evenly.
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 400 292" width="100%" role="img" aria-labelledby="rl-sc-t rl-sc-d">
  <title id="rl-sc-t">A sliding window counter</title>
  <desc id="rl-sc-d">
    Two one-minute windows side by side. The previous minute had 80 requests, drawn as an evenly
    filled block. We are 40 percent of the way into the current minute, which has 30 requests so
    far. The sliding window covers the last 60 seconds, so it overlaps 60 percent of the previous
    minute: 48 of its 80 requests still count and 32 have slid out. The estimate is 80 times 0.6
    plus 30, which is 78, below the limit of 100, so the request is allowed.
  </desc>

  <g font-size="19" text-anchor="middle">
    <text x="110" y="26" font-weight="600" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">previous minute: 80</text>
    <text x="290" y="26" font-weight="600" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">this minute: 30</text>
  </g>

  <!-- The sliding window: the last 60 s, from 0.4 of a window back into the previous one -->
  <rect x="92" y="40" width="180" height="150" rx="4" style="fill: var(--viz-flow-soft)" />
  <line x1="92" y1="40" x2="92" y2="190" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5 4" style="stroke: var(--viz-flow)" />
  <line x1="272" y1="40" x2="272" y2="190" stroke-width="2" style="stroke: var(--viz-flow)" />

  <!-- Previous minute, evenly spread: the part that slid out, and the part still counted -->
  <rect x="20" y="110" width="72" height="80" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 3" style="stroke: var(--viz-muted)" />
  <rect x="92" y="110" width="108" height="80" stroke-width="1.5" style="fill: var(--viz-flow-soft); stroke: var(--viz-flow)" />
  <text x="56" y="156" font-size="19" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">32 out</text>
  <text x="146" y="156" font-size="19" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">48 in</text>

  <!-- Current minute so far -->
  <rect x="200" y="140" width="72" height="50" stroke-width="1.5" style="fill: var(--viz-flow-soft); stroke: var(--viz-flow)" />
  <text x="236" y="172" font-size="19" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">30</text>

  <line x1="200" y1="40" x2="200" y2="190" stroke-width="1.5" style="stroke: var(--viz-muted)" />
  <line x1="20" y1="190" x2="380" y2="190" stroke-width="2" style="stroke: var(--viz-stroke)" />
  <g font-size="19" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">
    <text x="20" y="214" text-anchor="start">0 s</text>
    <text x="200" y="214">60 s</text>
    <text x="272" y="214" font-weight="600" style="fill: var(--viz-flow)">now</text>
    <text x="380" y="214" text-anchor="end">120 s</text>
  </g>

  <text x="200" y="252" font-size="19" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">80 × 0.6 + 30 = 78</text>
  <text x="200" y="280" font-size="19" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-ok)">under the limit of 100: allowed</text>
</svg>
